# Shape geometry, curved outline reached SQUARE-ON (engine backlog 14/16;
# DISCREPANCIES `SHAPE-AWARE-GEOMETRY`). Unpinned, so the return edge `pe -> net` is pushed
# into the side channel and arrives on the ellipse horizontally instead of
# along a ray from the centre — the touch-down path 210/211/212 never take
# (210 is unpinned but fans out only forward; 211/212 are pinned and purely
# diagonal). Parse model unaffected; tools/shape-check.js asserts the
# geometry.
#
# Repurposed: this case was `213-shape-cloud-geometry`, and
# its cloud-specific half — an outline drawn OUTSIDE its box (rx=w/2+10,
# ry=h/2+8), so a bounding-box clip stopped the edge under the fill — was
# deleted with the shape, not lost: no registered shape is drawn outside its
# box any more, so there is nothing left to assert. The half that survives is
# the back edge and its square-on touch-down, which no other case covers.
figdown 0.2 flowchart
node ce "CE router"
node net "Transit provider\nbackbone" shape=ellipse
node pe "PE router"
flow down
flowline ce -> net
flowline net -> pe
flowline pe -> net
